berkeley-principles-4.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: P3 (S3): "perceive" is taken as x is something we immediately perceive: the direct content of awareness, which is only our own ideas in P3 and as x is something we perceive by sense: a thing (house, river) that sense-perception is of where perceived_by_sense is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C1 (S3) does not follow (berkeley-principles-4.logic.r1.sense1)
